<DocLayout
  title="Support, Pretty Good Video Coaching"
  description="Get help with Pretty Good Video Coaching, the iPhone app for frame-accurate movement analysis."
>
  <h1>Support</h1>
  <p class="doc-updated">Pretty Good Video Coaching for iPhone</p>

  <p>
    Questions, problems, and requests all go to the same place:
    <a href="mailto:tom@prettygoodsoftware.llc">tom@prettygoodsoftware.llc</a>.
    You'll be talking to the developer.
  </p>
  <p>
    If something went wrong, include your iPhone model, your iOS version, and
    what you were doing when it happened. A screen recording helps more than a
    description.
  </p>

  <h2>Common questions</h2>

  <h3>Where are my videos?</h3>
  <p>
    On your iPhone, inside the app, nowhere else. The app has no accounts and
    no cloud. That also means deleting the app deletes everything in it, so
    export anything you want to keep first.
  </p>

  <h3>How do I get a clip out of the app?</h3>
  <p>
    Open the clip and use Share to export a flat video, your narration,
    drawings, and zoom baked in, or build a PDF report from marked moments.
    Both go anywhere Messages, Mail, or Files can reach.
  </p>

  <h3>Does the person I send it to need the app?</h3>
  <p>No. Exported videos and reports are ordinary files.</p>

  <h3>What does the app require?</h3>
  <p>
    An iPhone running iOS 17 or later. Camera, microphone, and photo-library
    access are each optional, the app asks only when a feature needs one.
  </p>

  <h2>Privacy</h2>
  <p>
    The short version: the app collects nothing.
    The long version is on the <a href="/privacy">privacy page</a>.
  </p>
</DocLayout>
